{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>But if the servant shall say, say.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory derived from this doubling of expression: until he says and repeats. 'The servant' — when he is a servant, excluding one who says so at the end, who is not a servant." "<b>I love my master.</b> His master loves him and he does not love his master — he is not bored through the ear. He loves his master and his master does not love him — he is not bored through the ear, as it is said (Deuteronomy 15:16): ״כי טוב לו עמך״ — 'because it is well with him with you.' His master is ill and he is not ill — he is not bored through the ear, as it is said: ״עמך״ — 'with you.' He is ill and his master is not ill — he is not bored through the ear, as it is said: ״כי טוב לו״ — 'because it is well with him.'" "<b>My wife and my children.</b> If he has no wife and children, he is not bored through the ear. If he said at the beginning of the six years and not at the end of the six years, he is not bored through the ear, for we require it adjacent to departure."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:05.546833285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}